            <ArticleTitle>Managing the transition to CFC-free inhalers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>248-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Asthma inhalers which use CFC propellants will be replaced by CFC-free devices within three years. Research suggests that inflammation in the small airways is often inadequately treated. CFC-free steroid-based inhalers appear to increase total lung deposition and peripheral lung penetration.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
